00:30:51.056 --> 00:30:53.840
of our engineering program
at the university of Arizona.

00:30:53.840 --> 00:30:55.770
And it's good to keep in mind

00:30:55.770 --> 00:30:57.900
that every institution
is going to be different

00:30:57.900 --> 00:31:02.040
in terms of their process
and the programs they offer.

00:31:02.040 --> 00:31:04.920
But as we mentioned,
you know, the cool thing

00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:06.670
about this field is that you can come out

00:31:06.670 --> 00:31:08.380
from a variety of different backgrounds.

00:31:08.380 --> 00:31:10.930
So I loved Ayelet's advice
about having an open mind.

00:31:10.930 --> 00:31:13.070
And I think that is super important

00:31:13.070 --> 00:31:16.340
as you're going through
your college search process

00:31:16.340 --> 00:31:18.500
as you're thinking about
what you want to major in.

00:31:18.500 --> 00:31:23.320
And it is okay as a high school
student to not know today

00:31:23.320 --> 00:31:26.070
or when you're applying
what exactly you want to do

00:31:26.070 --> 00:31:27.140
for the next four years.

00:31:27.140 --> 00:31:29.770
So that's one of my biggest
pieces of advice too

00:31:29.770 --> 00:31:33.090
is to just be curious, have an open-minded

00:31:33.090 --> 00:31:35.930
and pursue the things
that you really enjoy.

00:31:35.930 --> 00:31:38.610
So the way our program at
the university of Arizona

00:31:38.610 --> 00:31:40.810
is set up in our engineering school

00:31:40.810 --> 00:31:42.810
is actually all of our
engineering students

00:31:42.810 --> 00:31:44.350
